.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt ZFS-ALLOW 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zfs-allow
.Nd terminal UI and CLI for ZFS delegated administration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl list
.Op Fl json
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl add Ar who
.Fl perms Ar perms
.Op Fl scope Ar scope
.Op Fl n | Fl y | Fl check
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl remove Ar who
.Op Fl perms Ar perms
.Op Fl scope Ar scope
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl n | Fl y | Fl check
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl effective Ar user
.Op Fl json
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl where Ar who
.Op Fl json
.Nm
.Fl dump
.Op Fl r
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl restore Ar file
.Op Fl n | Fl y | Fl check
.Nm
.Fl catalogue
.Op Fl json
.Nm
.Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a front-end for
.Xr zfs-allow 8 :
it shows the delegated permissions of a dataset the way
.Ql zfs allow
prints them, lets you edit them as a checklist in which every permission is
described, and turns the edits into the exact
.Ql zfs allow
and
.Ql zfs unallow
commands, shown for review before they run.
Pre-flight checks point out what the commands will not achieve: a
.Sy create
without
.Sy mount ,
.Va vfs.usermount
set to 0, a mount point the grantee cannot create directories in, and what an
unprivileged operator may not do.
.Pp
Without options
.Nm
starts the interactive editor on
.Ar dataset ;
without a dataset it first shows a picker of every file system and volume,
with the dataset of the current directory preselected.
The options below are the non-interactive modes, for scripts and
configuration management; there
.Ar dataset
defaults to the one the current directory is on.
.Ar dataset
is a dataset name, or a path on a ZFS file system
.Pq the dataset holding it is used .
.Ss Model
A dataset's delegations consist of
.Bl -tag -width "create-time" -compact
.It entries
a user, a group or
.Sy everyone ,
with the permissions that apply to the dataset itself
.Pq Ql zfs allow -l
and the permissions that apply to its descendants
.Pq Ql zfs allow -d ;
.Ql zfs allow
prints their intersection as
.Dq Local+Descendent ;
.It sets
named bundles
.Pq Ar @name
that entries on this dataset and its descendants can refer to;
.It create-time
permissions granted locally to whoever creates a new descendant file system.
.El
.Pp
Entries of an ancestor that apply to descendants also apply here; the
interactive
.Ic i
key lists them, and
.Fl effective
takes them into account.
.Ss Interactive keys
.Bl -tag -width "ctrl+s, F10" -compact
.It Ic enter , e
edit the entry under the cursor
.It Ic a
add an entry, create-time permissions or a permission set
.It Ic d
delete the entry
.It Ic R
revoke the entry on this dataset and every descendant
.Pq Ql zfs unallow -r
.It Ic A
apply: show the commands and the pre-flight notes, then run them
.It Ic u , r
undo the last edit; reload from the kernel
.It Ic E
effective permissions of a user here, with every source
.It Ic i
the ancestors' delegations
.It Ic D
switch dataset
.It Ic q , esc
back to the dataset list when the session started there, otherwise quit
.It Ic ? , h
help, key list
.El
.Pp
In the editor:
.Ic /
filters the permissions by name or description,
.Ic space
toggles one permission (on a group header: the whole group),
.Ic enter
toggles and moves down,
.Ic a
and
.Ic n
select all or none of the shown permissions,
.Ic p
loads a preset,
.Ic x
shows the permissions
.Fx
refuses,
.Ic ctrl+s
confirms and
.Ic esc
cancels.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl list
Print the delegations of the dataset and of every ancestor that delegates
anything, in
.Ql zfs allow
format.
.It Fl add Ar who Fl perms Ar perms
Grant
.Ar perms
to
.Ar who .
.Ar who
is
.Ar user:NAME ,
.Ar group:NAME ,
.Sy everyone ,
.Ar @SET
.Pq define or extend a permission set
or
.Sy create-time .
.Ar perms
is a comma-separated list of permission names, permission sets
.Pq Ar @SET
and presets
.Pq Ar +PRESET ;
.Fl catalogue
lists them all.
.It Fl remove Ar who Op Fl perms Ar perms
Revoke
.Ar perms
.Pq or everything without Fl perms
from
.Ar who .
With
.Fl r
the revocation is done with
.Ql zfs unallow -r ,
on the dataset and every descendant.
.It Fl scope Ar scope
With
.Fl add
and
.Fl remove :
.Sy both
.Pq the default: the dataset and its descendants, Ql zfs allow No without Fl l No or Fl d ,
.Sy local
.Pq Fl l
or
.Sy descendants
.Pq Fl d .
.It Fl n
Print the
.Ql zfs
commands and the pre-flight notes without running them.
.It Fl y
Run the commands without asking.
.It Fl check
Dry run that exits 3 if anything would change and 0 if nothing would.
.It Fl effective Ar user
Print what
.Ar user
may do on the dataset: their own entries, their groups',
.Sy everyone Ns 's ,
and the descendant entries of every ancestor, with permission sets expanded
and every source listed.
.It Fl where Ar who
List every dataset on the system that delegates anything to
.Ar who .
.It Fl dump
Print a JSON snapshot of the dataset's delegations; with
.Fl r
of every descendant's too.
.It Fl restore Ar file
Bring every dataset recorded in a
.Fl dump
snapshot back to the recorded delegations; datasets that no longer exist are
skipped with a warning.
.Fl n ,
.Fl y
and
.Fl check
apply.
.It Fl catalogue
Print every permission with its kind
.Pq subcommand, other, property ,
group and description, and the presets.
.It Fl json
JSON output for
.Fl list ,
.Fl effective ,
.Fl where ,
.Fl catalogue
and
.Fl n .
.It Fl lenient
Accept permission names that are not in the catalogue
.Pq a newer OpenZFS may know more .
.It Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on error
.Pq including a refused Ql zfs No command ;
2 when the confirmation was declined; 3 when
.Fl check
found pending changes.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Preview the commands that give
.Sy bob
the snapshot preset plus
.Sy send
on his home dataset:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zfs-allow -add user:bob -perms +snapshots,send -n tank/home/bob
zfs allow -u bob bookmark,destroy,diff,hold,mount,release,rollback,send,snapshot tank/home/bob
note: vfs.usermount is 0: unprivileged users cannot mount, so mount and everything that needs it ... will fail
.Ed
.Pp
Revoke everything from a departed user on a whole subtree:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfs-allow -remove user:bob -r -y tank/home
.Ed
.Pp
Keep the delegations of a subtree under configuration management:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfs-allow -dump -r tank/home > delegations.json
# zfs-allow -restore delegations.json -check || zfs-allow -restore delegations.json -y
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr facl 1 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr zfs-allow 8
.Sh CAVEATS
Delegated permissions never override the mount point: to create file systems a
user also needs to create directories in the parent's mount point
.Pq chown it, or grant Sy add_subdirectory No with an NFSv4 ACL .
Unprivileged mounting needs
.Va vfs.usermount Ns =1 .
.Pp
An unprivileged user who holds the
.Sy allow
permission can delegate what they hold themselves, but can
.Ql zfs unallow
only their own entries and cannot define permission sets; the pre-flight
says so before the commands run.
.Pp
.Sy mlslabel
and
.Sy zoned
are refused on
.Fx
.Pq Dq operation not applicable to datasets of this type ,
the same message an unknown permission name gets.
.Pp
.Ql zfs allow
has no machine-readable output;
.Nm
parses its text, which has been stable since Solaris.
